# text = Which , you see , Pip ," said Joe , pausing in his meditative raking of the fire , and looking at me said Joe , with a judicial touch or two of the poker on the top bar I didn't see ; but I didn't say so Joe pursued I saw that , and said so Joe recited this couplet with such manifest pride and careful perspicuity , that I asked him if he had made it himself said Joe Joe's blue eyes turned a little watery ; he rubbed , first one of them , and then the other , in a most uncongenial and uncomfortable manner , with the round knob on the top of the poker said Joe Joe looked firmly at me , as if he knew I was not going to agree with him I could not help looking at the fire , in an obvious state of doubt Joe tapped the top bar with the poker after every word following I could think of nothing better to say than returned Joe , catching me up I sagaciously observed , if it didn't signify to him , to whom did it signify assented Joe Joe pursued with a countenance expressive of seeing something very nasty indeed Not exactly relishing this , I said he returned with tender simplicity I broke out crying and begging pardon , and hugged Joe round the neck : who dropped the poker to hug me , and to say When this little interruption was over , Joe resumed He had taken up the poker again ; without which , I doubt if he could have proceeded in his demonstration I was startled , for I had some shadowy idea ( and I am afraid I must add , hope ) that Joe had divorced her in a favour of the Lords of the Admiralty , or Treasury said Joe Joe continued I was going to retort with an inquiry , and had got as far as when Joe stopped me Joe sank his voice to a whisper and glanced at the door Joe pronounced this word , as if it began with at least twelve capital Bs said Joe , passing the poker into his left hand , that he might feel his whisker ; and I had no hope of him whenever he took to that placid occupation I asked , in some hope of bringing him to a stand .
