# text = My sister catching him in the act , he drew the back of his hand across his nose with his usual conciliatory air on such occasions , and looked at her said my sister , in her snappish way Joe politely hinted said my sister said Joe returned my sister said my sister , shaking her head at me as an encouragement to be extremely light and sportive I had heard of Miss Havisham up town - everybody for miles round , had heard of Miss Havisham up town - as an immensely rich and grim lady who lived in a large and dismal house barricaded against robbers , and who led a life of seclusion said Joe , astounded cried my sister Joe again politely hinted in a tone of the deepest reproach , as if he were the most callous of nephews , " then mention this boy , standing Prancing here " - which I solemnly declare I was not doing cried Uncle Pumblechook said my sister , still in a reproachful manner , while Joe apologetically drew the back of his hand across and across his nose cried my sister , casting off her bonnet in sudden desperation With that , she pounced upon me , like an eagle on a lamb , and my face was squeezed into wooden bowls in sinks , and my head was put under taps of water-butts , and I was soaped , and kneaded , and towelled , and thumped , and harrowed , and rasped , until I really was quite beside myself . ( I may here remark that I suppose myself to be better acquainted than any living authority , with the ridgy effect of a wedding-ring , passing unsympathetically over the human countenance .)
