# text = In her other hand she had a crutch-headed stick on which she leaned , and she looked like the Witch of the place said she , pointing to the long table with her stick With some vague misgiving that she might get upon the table then and there and die at once , the complete realization of the ghastly waxwork at the Fair , I shrank under her touch she asked me , again pointing with her stick She looked all round the room in a glaring manner , and then said , leaning on me while her hand twitched my shoulder I made out from this , that the work I had to do , was to walk Miss Havisham round and round the room .
