# text = The Hall was a queer place , I thought , with higher pews in it than a church - and with people hanging over the pews looking on - and with mighty Justices ( one with a powdered head ) leaning back in chairs , with folded arms , or taking snuff , or going to sleep , or writing , or reading the newspapers - and with some shining black portraits on the walls , which my unartistic eye regarded as a composition of hardbake and sticking-plaister .
