# text = Utterly preposterous as his cravat was , and as his collars were , I was conscious of a sort of dignity in the look resumed Joe said Joe , with his old air of lucid exposition I was so unwilling to see the look again , that I made no remonstrance against this tone pursued Joe whenever he subsided into affection , he called me Pip , and whenever he relapsed into politeness he called me Sir said Joe , going down a new track said Joe , slightly tossing his head Joe sat and rolled his eyes at the ceiling said Joe , looking at me as if I were a long way off replied Joe , with an air of legal formality , as if he were making his will I felt my face fire up as I looked at Joe .
