# text = For all these reasons ( I told Wemmick ), and because he was my young companion and friend , and I had a great affection for him , I wished my own good fortune to reflect some rays upon him , and therefore I sought advice from Wemmick's experience and knowledge of men and affairs , how I could best try with my resources to help Herbert to some present income - say of a hundred a year , to keep him in good hope and heart - and gradually to buy him on to some small partnership .
