# text = I faltered again said the Convict With my heart beating like a heavy hammer of disordered action , I rose out of my chair , and stood with my hand upon the back of it , looking wildly at him he went on All the truth of my position came flashing on me ; and its disappointments , dangers , disgraces , consequences of all kinds , rushed in in such a multitude that I was borne down by them and had to struggle for every breath I drew he resumed I could not have spoken one word , though it had been to save my life .
